1
00:00:09,774 --> 00:00:11,101
It looks like a gift.

2
00:00:11,901 --> 00:00:16,200
OpenAI says more than 1 billion people use it every week.

3
00:00:16,200 --> 00:00:18,462
The vast majority pay nothing.

4
00:00:19,362 --> 00:00:22,228
So… what are you paying with?

5
00:00:30,528 --> 00:00:32,915
November 30, 2022.

6
00:00:32,915 --> 00:00:35,169
ChatGPT launches.

7
00:00:35,169 --> 00:00:35,832
Free.

8
00:00:36,132 --> 00:00:38,631
Critics called it unreliable.

9
00:00:38,631 --> 00:00:41,302
1 million users came in 5 days.

10
00:00:41,602 --> 00:00:42,472
Why free?

11
00:00:42,772 --> 00:00:47,072
“We are excited to introduce ChatGPT to get users’ feedback…”

12
00:00:48,072 --> 00:00:50,292
And the next model, GPT-4?

13
00:00:50,292 --> 00:00:51,659
Already trained.

14
00:00:51,659 --> 00:00:54,306
3 months before you said hello.

15
00:00:54,706 --> 00:00:55,838
Scale built it.

16
00:00:55,838 --> 00:00:58,782
Bigger models, more data, more compute.

17
00:00:58,782 --> 00:01:00,216
Predictably better.

18
00:01:00,516 --> 00:01:02,433
Then OpenAI refined it.

19
00:01:02,683 --> 00:01:06,468
“…including feedback submitted by ChatGPT users…”

20
00:01:06,768 --> 00:01:09,460
The free product was shaping the next one.

21
00:01:09,760 --> 00:01:14,958
For the record: the documents mention user feedback and flagged answers.

22
00:01:14,958 --> 00:01:16,041
Not every chat.

23
00:01:18,441 --> 00:01:21,578
It has a name: the data flywheel.

24
00:01:21,878 --> 00:01:22,733
You use it.

25
00:01:24,051 --> 00:01:25,784
Your feedback becomes signal.

26
00:01:28,554 --> 00:01:29,961
The model improves.

27
00:01:29,961 --> 00:01:31,220
More people come.

28
00:01:31,520 --> 00:01:33,085
Even your thumbs-up counts.

29
00:01:33,335 --> 00:01:39,308
“…an additional reward signal based on user feedback—thumbs-up and thumbs-down data

30
00:01:39,308 --> 00:01:40,316
from ChatGPT.”

31
00:01:40,616 --> 00:01:44,917
It helped make the model so flattering that OpenAI rolled the update back.

32
00:01:45,217 --> 00:01:46,915
You're not just the customer.

33
00:01:46,915 --> 00:01:48,378
You're part of the wheel.

34
00:01:50,578 --> 00:01:52,701
Startups rushed to wrap the models.

35
00:01:53,001 --> 00:01:55,767
Then ChatGPT learned to read PDFs.

36
00:01:56,067 --> 00:01:59,348
One reaction: “Many startups just died today.”

37
00:01:59,648 --> 00:02:02,789
For the record: a reaction, not a count.

38
00:02:02,789 --> 00:02:04,909
Thin wrappers felt it most.

39
00:02:04,909 --> 00:02:08,129
Strong companies got squeezed, or bought.

40
00:02:08,429 --> 00:02:13,465
Sam Altman's warning: bet that the models won't improve, and you'll get steamrolled.

41
00:02:13,765 --> 00:02:15,342
Each model opens doors.

42
00:02:15,342 --> 00:02:17,536
The next release can close them.

43
00:02:19,636 --> 00:02:21,357
The wheel reaches the coders.

44
00:02:21,657 --> 00:02:23,696
Then the memos came.

45
00:02:23,696 --> 00:02:24,410
Use AI.

46
00:02:25,710 --> 00:02:31,230
In 2023, AI could solve about 2% of real GitHub issues on a benchmark.

47
00:02:31,530 --> 00:02:38,076
By February 2026, Anthropic reported about 80%, for Claude Opus 4.6.

48
00:02:38,376 --> 00:02:44,107
Then Claude Opus 5.5, which Anthropic puts at the level of its larger Fable model,

49
00:02:44,107 --> 00:02:45,016
on most work.

50
00:02:45,316 --> 00:02:47,850
And your code, on personal plans?

51
00:02:48,150 --> 00:02:53,554
“We believe the future of AI-assisted development depends on real-world interaction

52
00:02:53,554 --> 00:02:55,573
data from developers like you.”

53
00:02:58,873 --> 00:03:01,145
So why is it nearly free?

54
00:03:01,445 --> 00:03:03,286
Investor billions.

55
00:03:03,286 --> 00:03:05,026
A race for users.

56
00:03:05,026 --> 00:03:05,435
Ads.

57
00:03:05,435 --> 00:03:06,867
Falling costs.

58
00:03:07,167 --> 00:03:09,895
And part of the price is paid in data.

59
00:03:11,195 --> 00:03:12,132
Yours.

60
00:03:14,032 --> 00:03:16,630
For the record: there is a switch.

61
00:03:16,930 --> 00:03:19,177
Most people never touch their defaults.

62
00:03:19,477 --> 00:03:20,488
It's a trade.

63
00:03:20,488 --> 00:03:21,810
Often a good one.

64
00:03:22,210 --> 00:03:24,483
So our app just calls the model—

65
00:03:24,483 --> 00:03:29,204
But if your plan is a thin wrapper around someone else's model...

66
00:03:29,204 --> 00:03:29,712
please.

67
00:03:29,712 --> 00:03:30,075
Wait.

68
00:03:30,375 --> 00:03:31,424
The wheel won't.

69
00:03:35,424 --> 00:03:36,234
Still.

70
00:03:36,234 --> 00:03:37,448
Go ahead.

71
00:03:37,448 --> 00:03:38,258
Build.

72
00:03:38,258 --> 00:03:39,877
Raise money.

73
00:03:39,877 --> 00:03:40,552
Ship.

74
00:03:40,852 --> 00:03:43,802
But your biggest asset isn't on that list.

75
00:03:44,202 --> 00:03:45,333
Your attention.

76
00:03:45,333 --> 00:03:49,857
We now stay on one screen about 47 seconds before switching.

77
00:03:49,857 --> 00:03:50,536
Guard it.

78
00:03:52,828 --> 00:03:53,579
Your mind.

79
00:03:53,579 --> 00:03:59,583
In Anthropic's own trial, coders learning with AI scored 17 points lower on what

80
00:03:59,583 --> 00:04:01,084
they'd just learned.

81
00:04:01,084 --> 00:04:01,759
Train it.

82
00:04:03,921 --> 00:04:06,431
Your body, your mental health.

83
00:04:06,431 --> 00:04:11,451
People who exercise report 43% fewer bad mental-health days.

84
00:04:11,451 --> 00:04:12,120
Move it.

85
00:04:14,457 --> 00:04:16,666
No release will update you.

86
00:04:16,666 --> 00:04:17,730
Only you can.

87
00:04:19,730 --> 00:04:21,268
Invest consciously.

